  "photoGrounding": "The supplied rooftop photos organize local rubbed joints, branching repairs, water/mineral remnants and warm old mortar. They are viewed as material evidence; no photograph is downscaled into an atlas.",
  "referenceReading": [
    "The station pillar and ground use many close grey-green levels and small adjoining hard-edged mineral fragments. Large pillar light/dark changes primarily come from physical lighting, so this albedo uses restrained material differences.",
    "The earlier 05 solid 25–46 px light/dark islands read as camouflage. 06 discards their BOUNDARIES and stamp outlines entirely, rather than shrinking or recolouring them."
