  "paintChanges": [
    "Twelve low-saturation grey-green pigments are planned per field. The substrate and adjacent levels at ±4/8 RGB dominate; ±12/16 levels remain context layers, and deepest fissure, mineral pale and warm mortar are rare local accents.",
    "Every short 2–7 px fragment gets a fresh outline, irregular row offsets, and a local adjoining-tone walk. Chains join unevenly but do not fill a macro polygon.",
    "Ground density follows separate repair, washing and damp sites. Several skewed quiet regions retain continuous substrate. North and south keep independent fissure/washing layouts and broken structural grout.",
    "Wall painting emphasizes short broken vertical mineral runoff and small lime erosion. Unequal quiet windows and denser local weathering sites avoid an even whole-wall dot field or a continuous dark foot stripe.",
    "Cap and cement have multiple close mineral remnants and bounded old-layer clusters; rare edge glints and narrow fissures retain material identity.",
    "Only six atlas regions are repainted. Brick-red roofs, grey roofs, all metal/rust fields, erased Chinese signs and all other pixels remain exactly equal to 05."
  ],
